            <ArticleTitle>Bleeding risk in endoscopic retrograde cholangiopancreatography. Impact of the use of antithrombotic drugs.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>202-210</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.17235/reed.2017.4358/2016</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIMS" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To analyze the risk factors for hemorrhage during endoscopic retrograde cholangiopancreatography and the impact of antithrombotic drugs.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIAL AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Data sources: papers indexed in PubMed have been reviewed, as well as those found during the analysis of the bibliography of meta-analysis and reviews.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SELECTION CRITERIA" NlmCategory="METHODS">the references have been firstly evaluated by review of the abstract. After selecting the most significant articles (mainly randomized trials and well-designed case series) these have been deeply analyzed. Evaluation of the studies and synthesis: criteria by the Oxford Centre for Evidence-Based Medicine have been used for the analysis of the references and elaboration of evidence levels.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Seven hundred and sixty-five references were found, 753 in PubMed and the Cochrane Library. Twelve studies were selected during the analysis of other published articles (systematic reviews, meta-analysis and clinical practice guidelines). After analyzing the title or the abstract, 655 studies were excluded. Finally, 83 high quality trials or descriptive studies have been included in the analysis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Seven conclusions regarding the risk factors for bleeding and the impact of antithrombotic drugs have been defined.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
